================================================================================
TEST T44968 -- CLI show mirror interface direction set to receive
================================================================================
Run:      2026-10-09 08:56-09:03 NZ (box local; both device clocks set to box local time
          before the run, so device and host stamps are directly comparable)
Bench:    tb277, consoles u2, u3, u5; Test Engineer bidhanc@bidhanc-dl
Tester:   bench-runner
Graded:   tester
Case:     AWP-5317, objective "set a port mirror's direction to receive and confirm, from
          the CLI and on the wire, that only received traffic is copied", 4 steps
Build:    swi_c  sin_x96056-20260921-9 (x960-tb277.rel, build Mon Sep 21 11:25:03 UTC 2026)
          swi_b  sin_x96056-20260921-9
Configs:  swi_c.cfg, swi_b.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- `direction receive` is reported correctly by both show commands and copies
         ONLY the frames the DUT receives on the monitored port, the exact inverse of
         `direction transmit` on identical cabling.
      command accepted on destination .... yes      (entered on port1.0.10 naming port1.0.48)
      show mirror ....................... correct  (dest port1.0.10, receive, src port1.0.48)
      show mirror interface <src> ....... correct
      ingress frames copied ............. 6        (echo requests seen at the destination)
      egress frames copied .............. 0        (echo replies correctly NOT copied)
      inverse of transmit ............... yes      (6/0 here against 0/6 for transmit)
      forwarding undisturbed ............ yes      (ping 6/6, 0% loss while mirroring)
CAVEAT:  The mirror did not take effect on first application and copied nothing until the
         destination port was bounced. That is recorded below as a defect of mirror
         RE-APPLICATION, not of `direction receive`, which behaved correctly once programmed.
         A second defect found here -- an in-place direction change being silently ignored --
         means `show mirror` is not evidence of what the dataplane is doing on this platform.
         This verdict therefore rests entirely on captured frames.

